Which check of the passive match said no

The candidates are turned away by the passive match -- the one that asks
whether the nub is the thing the personality wants.  It asks in four places:
the name, the location, the properties and the existence of a property.
Which of them said no is the difference between a personality that wanted
another board and one that wanted this one and was asked for the wrong name.

So the match says which check said no: x is its number (0 is none, 4 the
name, 6 the properties), and after it what was wanted and what the nub is
called.  The name is the one that matters here: the board takes the name
of its device tree, and a personality written for another board asks for
that other name.

